course: dictionary
lesson: 6624
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word note is one of them. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right. «In Ohio, a teacher hands Everett a note in front of everyone saying his family owes $12.» A note here is a short written message, because it is handed over and it says something.
explain: «Blowing too hard makes a recorder jump up to a shrill squeal; a soft, steady breath gives a clear note.» Here a note is one sound in music. The clues are recorder, breath and clear, which are all about sound.
explain: To note is a verb. «She noted that the door was open» means she noticed it. Try the meaning in the sentence: she noticed that the door was open. It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Note has more than one meaning, so check the clues around it.
fact: A note can be a short written message, or a piece of paper money, like a 10-pound note.
fact: A note can be one sound in music, and music notes have names from A to G.
fact: To note means to write something down, or to notice it.
fact: Notes you write to remember things are also called notes, like when you take notes in class.
exercise: «A teacher hands Everett a note saying his family owes money.» What does note mean here? | * A written message | A sound in music | A long, thin string on a guitar | To notice something
exercise: «A soft, steady breath gives a clear note.» What is a note in this sentence? | * One sound in music | A piece of paper money | A string on a guitar | A short message to a friend
exercise: «She noted that the door was open.» What does noted mean? | Closed | Painted | Wrote a letter | * Noticed
test: «I paid for my lunch with a 10-pound note.» What is a note in this sentence? | A stick to hit a drum | A sound in music | * A piece of paper money | A written message
test: «Mum left a sticky note on the fridge.» What does note mean here? | Paper money | To notice something | A sound in music | * A short written message to remember something
exam: «Notes sit both on the lines and in the spaces between them.» Which meaning of note fits here? | To notice something | Paper money | A short written message | * One sound in music, or the sign for it
